# Allow-list: the build context carries only what the Dockerfile copies and
# builds. Everything else (the repository's history, agent and fleet files,
# documents, local state, secrets) is not sent to the builder.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
!testdata/fixture/discount
!testdata/fixture/discount-clean
!testdata/fixture/unknown-author
!testdata/fixture/malicious-package
!testdata/fixture/osv-go-module
!testdata/fixture/spdx-licence
!testdata/fixture/project-health

# Inside an allowed directory, still never send these.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
# The documentation site (docs-site/Dockerfile) builds from the repository root:
# docs/, assets/ and README.md are its input, so they are not ignored. Its own
# build output stays out of the context.
**/node_modules
**/.next
docs-site/content
docs-site/public
docs-site/.source
